    "status": "proposed, unruled",
    "about": "interiorDay: the share of the built daylight level the rooms behind kit glass keep (1 = as built). Every shop front, the glass proof front too, keeps its interior at night under the city's shop cap of 0.3. Proposal, unruled: render r.Lumen.HardwareRayTracing.LightingMode 2 (hit lighting), so a pane's reflection lights what it hits from that surface's own material and the direct light instead of the surface cache, which has no skinned characters: without it a lead before a shop pane is missing from the reflection. Cost in principle: every reflection ray that hits evaluates its hit's material and direct lighting, so it grows with the reflecting pixels on screen and the materials they meet.",
